This is the default `timeZone` handed to every `Intl.DateTimeFormat` created through next-intl. The organizer pages then add their own explicit formatting on top — e.g. series/[id]/manage/page.tsx:311 `new Date(leg.startDate).toLocaleDateString(locale)` and payouts/page.tsx:298 `new Date(p.createdAt).toLocaleDateString('vi-VN')` — both of which silently re-apply the *browser* timezone, contradicting the server-side `Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh` default. Confidence 0.7 because the app is Vietnam-only in practice, so I cannot show a concrete mis-rendered date for a real user.

